      "writtenOn": "2023-09-20T08:15:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e For media case, \"export media interfaces until the services are available\", is this something you\u0027re planning for?\n\nI think this should be implemented in this way but I haven\u0027t checked the libbluetooth API how to determine if the API is ready. And also, we only observe crash caused by exposing GATT interface too early but not in media interface. So I\u0027ll leave it as a TODO task for now.\n\n\u003e  I was wondering if this is try for GATT case? I was expecting scanner and advertiser will be ready once the underlying Bluetooth stack is up.\n\nI\u0027m not sure about the libbluetooth API, but at the bottom line, we should only expose it **after** [init_profiles](https://source.corp.google.com/h/chromium/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/aosp/packages/modules/Bluetooth/upstream/system/gd/rust/linux/stack/src/bluetooth_gatt.rs;l\u003d1393?q\u003dsystem%2Fgd%2Frust%2Flinux%2Fstack%2Fsrc%2Fbluetooth_gatt.rs\u0026ss\u003dh%2Fchromium%2Fchromiumos%2Fcodesearch%2F%2B%2Frefs%2Fheads%2Fmain:src%2Faosp%2Fpackages%2Fmodules%2FBluetooth%2Fupstream%2F) is called, otherwise the self.gatt is None and cause panics in many API handler in unwrap. This is also what I did in the next CL.",
